Create a new endpoint on a deployment.

USAGE:
  scw searchdb endpoint create [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  [deployment-id]                                      ID of the deployment for which to create an endpoint
  [endpoint-spec.public]                               
  [endpoint-spec.private-network.private-network-id]   
  [region=fr-par]                                      Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config (fr-par)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for create
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use
